# Resolution
Fixed in commit 022cbee8ce3969f74c69f5587bf05925b3e721bb
(`Route completed MPU prune through metadata commands`).

The fix adds a row-shaped `DeleteCompletedMultipartUpload` metadata command
whose checksum covers the exact completed-MPU tombstone row. Completed-MPU
pruning and bucket-finalization cleanup now scan routed metadata PG acting sets
and remove each pruned tombstone through the metadata command apply path instead
of mutating only the PG primary directly. Partial apply is retryable through the
pending command mechanism, and the regression
`completed_multipart_prune_partial_command_retries_and_preserves_digest` verifies
that a failed prune can be retried and that later metadata commands on the PG do
not hit a digest mismatch.

# Summary
Introduced. The pre-existing pruning path was safe only while completed_multipart_uploads was outside the canonical digest. This commit made the table digest-covered without converting pruning to a command-consistent acting-set mutation or refreshing the digest after the local primary-only delete.
completed_multipart_uploads is now included in METADATA_DIGEST_TABLES, so changes to this table affect metadata_state_digest(). However, prune_completed_multipart_uploads_for_bucket_with_limit() is invoked after normal CompleteMultipartUpload processing and deletes old completed-MPU tombstones by calling metadata_pg(), which resolves only the primary node's PG. The delete is not applied to the acting set as a metadata command and does not refresh the affected replica's stored state_digest. For PGs whose digest gate is still active, the next metadata command runs metadata_state_digest_mismatch(), sees the changed completed_multipart_uploads table, and returns MetadataStateDigestMismatch instead of accepting the command. An authenticated writer can create an old completed MPU on a target PG, then complete enough newer MPUs on another PG to exceed the per-bucket retained tombstone limit and prune the old row, persistently denying subsequent writes/metadata operations on the target PG until administrative repair.

